@@ -4,4 +4,13 @@ Report stock levels from a CSV file with columns `name,qty,price`.
 
 ## Usage
 
-    python3 inventory.py items.csv [--min-qty N]
+    python3 inventory.py items.csv [--min-qty N] [--format {table,json}]
+
+- `--min-qty N` only report items with at least N in stock (default 0).
+- `--format table` (default) prints one aligned line per item.
+- `--format json` prints a JSON array of objects with keys `name`, `qty`
+  and `price`, sorted by name, and nothing else on stdout.
+
+Rows whose `qty` or `price` cannot be parsed are skipped, with a
+`skipping row N: ...` warning on stderr (N = 1-based data row number).
+An unknown format value is a usage error (exit status 2).
